Author: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date:   Fri Nov 13 18:33:18 2026 +0000

    Listing photos: the warmer runs once a quarter hour, and a stored photo never outlives its listing
    
    Owner's brief, 2026-11-13. Measured 2026-11-12: the photo-warmer Worker called /homes/api/warm 18 times a minute, about 85 CRM listing calls a minute day and night; the CRM's database ran out of connections (searches failed about 100 times at 7 AM and 200 at 11 AM ET).
    
    The throttle (idx-lib/photo.js, functions/homes/[[path]].js):
    - One run at a time: a lock in the bucket, moved only by a compare-and-swap. A call within 14 minutes of the last run does nothing, so the old Worker's 18 calls a minute become one run a quarter hour with no other change.
    - A run makes at most 16 listing calls (48 homes each, by price) and fetches at most 12 photos: 28 CRM calls a run, under 30 in any 10 minutes. Never from the edge cache, never retried. 429: wait its retry-after, end the run. 503 stale or any 5xx: end the run.
    - A copy already kept is never fetched again. Copies are named l/<listingKey>/<v>/<n>-<w>.webp from the CRM's photo link.
    - The CRM answers pages 1 to 100 only, so the old warmer (24 a page) only ever saw the newest 2,400 homes. The sweep goes by price and starts again from the last price at page 99.
    - workers/photo-warmer: the new Worker, one call every 15 minutes (cron */15).
    - idx-lib/crm.js: no CRM answer is cached at the edge longer than an hour (the AI reader's descriptions were cached a year); the warmer's calls skip the edge cache.
    
    The licence (CLAUDE.md non-negotiable 9):
    - Only the warmer stores, only for listings the CRM returned in the current sweep; a visitor's request never stores.
    - A removal sweep starts every 5 h 45 min. At its end every copy in the bucket whose listing or version it did not see is deleted, checked against the bucket itself. A changed version loses its old copies in the run that sees it. A sweep not finished in 6 hours is dropped.
    - Copies are served only while the last finished sweep is under 6 hours old, else the CRM's own link. A served copy is cached an hour at most.
    - The old hash-named copies (p/v1/, 2.81 GB): after the first finished sweep, those of listings it saw at that version are kept and tracked; all others are deleted.
    - tools/idx-test.mjs: "photo warmer HARD RULE" (a listing missing from the API has its copies deleted on the next sweep; it fails with the deletion removed), plus the lock, the 18-call burst, the 30-a-10-minutes limit, 429/503/500, serving and the old copies.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_012hytMouaajg3aWuepm8WSU

